  "posted_text": "🚆 Transportation\nMD HB0862 — Maryland Trains Now Need a Two-Person Crew\n\nMaryland law now requires that any railroad train used to transport freight has a crew of at least two individuals. Violations of this new rule carry a $25,000 fine. This change takes effect on October 1, 2026, but is contingent on similar legislation passing in New York, Pennsylvania, and Virginia. .. .... ..",
